breaking news in Missouri where at least  two people were killed in a mass  shooting outside a nightclub police  surrounded the nine Ultra Lounge in  Kansas City around 11:30 last night it's  believed they met a male shooter was one  of those people killed more than a dozen  others were injured Savannah Rudisill of  our Kansas City affiliate that's KC TV  she's near the scene good morning kids  city police are still investigating what  led up to the deadly shooting right now  we have a handful of officers right  outside of the club earlier this morning  just a few hours ago we had dozens of  different officers from different  agencies around the area they were  hosting a sold-out celebration party for  the Kansas City Chiefs conference  championship and then the night turned  to chaos the shooting started when the  gunman fired into a line of people  waiting to get in line at the club we  know that two people are dead one of  them is the shooter police tell us that  an armed security guard took down the  gunman we know 15 other people have gone  to area hospitals three of them are in  critical condition police say there were  a lot of witnesses to this they are  offering a $25,000 reward for any  information that leads to arrest for CBS  this morning Savannah Rudisill Kansas  City Missouri
 

